# Fuzz corpus files are arbitrary fuzzer-mutated bytes, not text: EOL normalization
# would silently rewrite a CR/LF-bearing seed (e.g. a `\r\n` literal) and change which
# input the seed represents. Mark them binary so their bytes are stored verbatim.
# The commit guard's final-newline policy honors `-text` too, so seeds keep their
# deliberately missing final newline.
seed/** -text
corpus/** -text
artifacts/** -text
